eams Engaging Staff and Teams Fostering Culture Change New Employees Getting Started Before You Start Your First Days and Weeks Your First Months Finding Your Way Policies Senior Leader Onboarding MIT's Structure and Governance MIT's Culture and Community Suggested Reading Leadership and Organization Development Retirees Health and Medical Plans 65 and Over Under 65 Medicare Prescription Drug Plan Continuing Care at MIT Health Dental Plan Flexible Spending Account Life Insurance HR Partners HR Partners Resource Guide Crisis Support External Career Counselors External Coaches, Consultants, and Trainers Layoffs Progressive Discipline Terminations and Offboarding HR HQ Events News Get Help In the Office Conference Rooms Safety and Security Recognition HR Infinite Mile Award Spot Appreciation Award Nomination Form Templates and Tools Reports Tech Help and Resources Events What's new Atlas HR team Contact Search Jobs Site Search Search Jobs at MIT Join us in building a better world. Our dynamic environment, distinct culture, and diverse community foster collaboration and excellence in every corner of the Institute. MIT employees enjoy an extensive range of benefits and resources that simply aren't found together anywhere else. If you’re ready to help us shape the future, there’s a place at MIT for your unique skills, experience, and goals. MIT has paused hiring for most non-essential positions, but we are actively seeking candidates for any positions that are currently posted. Search Jobs See open positions at MIT. Discover MIT Learn more about our full range of benefits designed to keep you healthy, provide work-life balance, build your long-term financial security, and more. Information for Applicants Have questions about applying for a position at MIT? Find answers here. MIT is an equal opportunity employer. We value diversity and strongly encourage applications from individuals from all identities and backgrounds. All qualified applicants will receive equitable consideration for employment based on their experience and qualifications, and will not be discriminated against on the basis of race, color, sex, sexual orientation, gender identity, pregnancy, religion, disability, age, genetic information, veteran status, or national or ethnic origin. See MIT's full policy on nondiscrimination. Know your rights. If you are a job seeker with a disability and require an accommodation in order to apply for one of our jobs, please contact us . MIT considers equivalent combinations of experience and education for certain jobs. All candidates who believe they possess equivalent experience and education are encouraged to apply. Employment is contingent upon the complete of a satisfactory background check. MIT is committed to providing for the safety and security of all members of our community. In accordance with the Clery Act, MIT publishes an Annual Security and Fire Safety Report. You may obtain the most recent copy of this report here or request a hard copy from the MIT Police. Labor Condition Application Notifications These US Department of Labor required notices serve as notice to Massachusetts Institute of Technology employees of applications for H-1B non-immigrants for certain academic and research positions. MIT HR Logo, return to homepage Human Resources Massachusetts Institute of Technology Building NE49-5000 600 Technology Square Cambridge, MA 02139 Contact Events Linkedin HR Team Accessibility Join us in building a better world. Search Term Search Search Jobs Forms & Resources Health Plans Institute Holidays Life Events MyLife Services"
