Teams Engaging Staff and Teams Fostering Culture Change New Employees Getting Started Before You Start Your First Days and Weeks Your First Months Finding Your Way Policies Senior Leader Onboarding MIT's Structure and Governance MIT's Culture and Community Suggested Reading Leadership and Organization Development Retirees Health and Medical Plans 65 and Over Under 65 Medicare Prescription Drug Plan Continuing Care at MIT Health Dental Plan Flexible Spending Account Life Insurance HR Partners HR Partners Resource Guide Crisis Support External Career Counselors External Coaches, Consultants, and Trainers Layoffs Progressive Discipline Terminations and Offboarding HR HQ Events News Get Help In the Office Conference Rooms Safety and Security Recognition HR Infinite Mile Award Spot Appreciation Award Nomination Form Templates and Tools Reports Tech Help and Resources Events What's new Atlas HR team Contact Search Jobs Site Search Search Home Your Career Your Career Learn & Grow Learn & Grow MIT values learning and growth both professionally and personally. See our opportunities to learn, discover, and chart your career at MIT. Investing in your professional development is one of the most impactful ways to advance your career and achieve personal satisfaction in your work. Human Resources provides a diverse range of in-person, virtual, online, self-paced, and consultative resources to help enhance individual and team effectiveness, foster deeper personal engagement in the work, and enhance overall job satisfaction. Upcoming Events Manager's Feedback Program Business Skills & Knowledge Tuesday, September 8, 2026 10:00 am to 12:00 pm NE49-5000 Register HR Partners Group Event Business Skills & Knowledge Wednesday, September 23, 2026 10:00 am to 11:30 am Online Register Networking/Storytelling for Your Career Career & Talent Development Thursday, September 24, 2026 1:00 pm to 3:00 pm NE49-5145B NE49-5145 L-Lab Register See all events For Managers Chart your development as a manager using these resources. Career Resources MIT provides comprehensive career development services to help you think about your career and development plan at the Institute, including workshops and individual consulting. Online Learning Resources Expand your knowledge through a variety of self-directed, just-in-time learning resources. Work-Life Webinars The Webinar Series from Work-Life provides research-based strategies and information to help you deal with a diverse array of work-life and wellbeing issues. Browse topics More Programs Available to Employees Search Inside Yourself Program The Search Inside Yourself Leadership Program focuses on mindfulness and emotional intelligence skills, rooted in neuroscience, with an aim of improving engagement and well-being at home and at work. In addition, participants will learn new skills and practical applications to reduce stress, increase resilience, develop greater self-awareness, improve communication, build empathy, and lead with compassion. Learn more and register. Insights into Management Thinking about becoming a manager? Insights into Management is a virtual training program that helps smooth the transition from individual contributor to management. Leader to Leader (L2L) The nationally recognized Leader to Leader (L2L) Program is a year-long cohort program that provides participants with dedicated time for reflection and self-discovery, theoretical and applied learning, and dialogue with fellow MIT leaders. Managers' Feedback Program MIT managers are invited to join this program on asking for, receiving, and using feedback to improve effectiveness and augment growth. MIT Management Executive Education programs Earn an Executive Certificate from MIT's Sloan School of Management by completing 4 short courses. MIT staff and spouses are eligible for a 15% discount with the code STAFF15 when registering with an mit.edu address. See a complete list of programs MIT Professional Education programs MIT Professional Education offers programs across a broad range of topic categories, levels of engagement, and time commitments. Eligible MIT employees may use their MIT Tuition Assistance Plan for online and on-campus courses. The Susan Vogt Leadership Development Program The Susan Vogt Leadership Development Program , sponsored by the Boston Consortium for Higher Education, is a management and leadership development program designed to foster collaboration and camaraderie in the next generation of leaders in higher education. Tuition assistance MIT provides tuition assistance to help you build or improve the skills you need to develop your career at MIT. Learn more about tuition assistance MIT HR Logo, return to homepage Human Resources Massachusetts Institute of Technology Building NE49-5000 600 Technology Square Cambridge, MA 02139 Contact Events Linkedin HR Team Accessibility Working together to build a better world. Search Term Search Search Jobs Forms & Resources Health Plans Institute Holidays Life Events MyLife Services"
    },
