Developing Your Staff and Teams Engaging Staff and Teams Fostering Culture Change New Employees Getting Started Before You Start Your First Days and Weeks Your First Months Finding Your Way Policies Senior Leader Onboarding MIT's Structure and Governance MIT's Culture and Community Suggested Reading Leadership and Organization Development Retirees Health and Medical Plans 65 and Over Under 65 Medicare Prescription Drug Plan Continuing Care at MIT Health Dental Plan Flexible Spending Account Life Insurance HR Partners HR Partners Resource Guide Crisis Support External Career Counselors External Coaches, Consultants, and Trainers Layoffs Progressive Discipline Terminations and Offboarding HR HQ Events News Get Help In the Office Conference Rooms Safety and Security Recognition HR Infinite Mile Award Spot Appreciation Award Nomination Form Templates and Tools Reports Tech Help and Resources Events What's new Atlas HR team Contact Search Jobs Site Search Search Home Your Career Learn & Grow Learn & Grow Management Foundations Cohort Program Management Foundations Cohort Program The Management Foundations Cohort Program (MFCP) equips new MIT people managers with the foundational leadership and management skills needed to excel in their roles. Now Accepting Applications The fall 2026 cohort application will be open through September 4, 2026 . Learn more about the program and apply below. About the Program The MFCP was developed to meet the needs of new managers (both those who are new to managing and those who are new to the Institute) and provide an opportunity for experienced managers to refresh their essential skills. Topics include giving and receiving feedback, building trust and effective communication with direct reports, understanding performance development and developing strategic decision-making and delegation abilities. Practice and discussion sessions are interspersed with interactive workshops over the course of several weeks. MFCP participants will learn and practice relevant and useful tools for managing themselves and their direct reports more effectively and efficiently. Features Cohort format to facilitate shared learning and peer engagement On-the-job application of program learning Tools and frameworks that participants can use to support their own growth and the development of their direct reports Practice and discussion sessions to consolidate learning and reinforce new skills and behaviors Schedule Fall 2026 sessions will take place in NE49-5000 (MIT Human Resources), on Zoom, and through online, self-guided courses. Session Date Time Learning Modality Attendance Program Orientation Thursday, October 8 9:30 - 11 a.m. In-person, NE49-5000 Required Module 1: Your Role as a Manager Self-paced to be completed by Thursday, October 15 1-hour course Online Required Module 2: Understand and Manage Your Emotions Self-paced to be completed by Thursday, October 15 1-hour course Online Required Discussion/Practice 1 Thursday, October 15 1 - 2:30 p.m. In-person, NE49-5000 Required Module 3: Receiving and Offering Feedback, Part I Tuesday, October 20 9:30 - 11:30 a.m. Zoom Required Discussion/Practice 2 Thursday, October 22 1 - 2:30 p.m. Zoom Optional Module 4: Building Trust Through Communication Tuesday, October 27 9:30 - 11:30 a.m. In-person, NE49-5000 Required Discussion/Practice 3 Thursday, October 29 1 - 2:30 p.m. Zoom Optional Module 5: Receiving and Offering Feedback, Part II Tuesday, November 3 9:30 - 11:30 a.m. In-person, NE49-5000 Required Discussion/Practice 4 Thursday, November 5 1 - 2:30 p.m. Zoom Optional Module 6: Decision-Making and Delegation for Managers Tuesday, November 10 9:30 - 11:30 a.m. Zoom Required Discussion/Practice 5 Thursday, November 12 1 - 2:30 p.m. Zoom Optional Module 7: Performance Reviews Self-paced to be completed by Thursday, November 19 1.5-hour course Online Required Discussion/Practice 6 Thursday, November 19 9:30 - 11 a.m. In-person, NE49-5000 Required Program Closing Thursday, November 19 11 a.m. - 12 p.m. In-person, NE49-5000 Required Applying to MFCP The fall 2026 cohort application will be open through September 4, 2026 . Please have your manager's support to participate in the program before applying. Application Form After you complete your application, your manager will be invited to complete a short form indicating their support for your participation in the program. Participants will be notified of their acceptance by September 11, 2026. MIT HR Logo, return to homepage Human Resources Massachusetts Institute of Technology Building NE49-5000 600 Technology Square Cambridge, MA 02139 Contact Events Linkedin HR Team Accessibility Working together to build a better world. Search Term Search Search Jobs Forms & Resources Health Plans Institute Holidays Life Events MyLife Services"
