s and strategies to become more adept in your interpersonal communication. Articles and Tools The Basics of Communicating with Others The Gourmet Chef's Guide to Giving Feedback Tips for Active Listening Designing and Facilitating Meetings Designing Meetings is about techniques and methods that help meetings run smoothly and groups work collaboratively. Articles and Tools The Basics of Designing & Facilitating Meetings Brainstorming Guidelines How and Why to Use a Meeting Agenda Tips for Recording Leading and Managing Others Leading and Managing Others is about how managers can be effective leaders of organizational change. When managers manage as leaders, they proactively take steps to lead a group towards a vision of the future. Articles and Tools The Basics of Managing as a Leader Build Relationships with Your Team through Coaching Five Don'ts for the Manager/Leader Self-Assessment for Managers as Leaders (Microsoft Word) Understanding the Culture of Your Organization (Microsoft Word) What is Coaching? Managing Change Change management is a set of ideas, strategies, and skills that can be applied to engage change effectively. Managing Change offers resources to help individuals and teams respond to and manage change more effectively at MIT. Articles and Tools The Basics of Managing Change Change Gauge Tool (Microsoft Word) Four Thoughts for Enabling Change Planning for Change: The Force Field Tool Working on Teams Teams share a commitment to a common purpose, mission and goals. Working on Teams offers tools and techniques to help both members and leaders of MIT teams work more cooperatively and effectively. Articles and Tools The Basics of Working on Teams Decision-Making Models Important Steps When Building a New Team Using the Stages of Team Development Permission to Distribute All Learning Topic materials are copyright © Massachusetts Institute of Technology, unless otherwise indicated. Please feel free to use our materials for non-commercial purposes only. We are happy to know that our materials can be useful to other individuals and organizations. We also request that the following reference, \"Developed by the Strategic Talent Development team, Human Resources, Massachusetts Institute of Technology (MIT)\" is included on the materials and that the primary author is referenced as well. Questions? Reach us at learn@mit.edu . Learn and Grow, Professionally and Personally Choose from a mix of role-based programs, skill-based workshops, and online resources to discover, learn, and grow in your career at MIT. What will you learn? MIT HR Logo, return to homepage Human Resources Massachusetts Institute of Technology Building NE49-5000 600 Technology Square Cambridge, MA 02139 Contact Events Linkedin HR Team Accessibility Working together to build a better world. Search Term Search Search Jobs Forms & Resources Health Plans Institute Holidays Life Events MyLife Services"
